WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.610
- Were you able to perform
on stage at all this summer?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.443
- Yes.

00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:07.080
You know so I went out
to yellow Springs Ohio,

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.470
to Dave Chappelle's.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.440
Dave Chappelle has a, like
a summer camp going on.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.535
Where it's performances that are COVID.

00:00:13.535 --> 00:00:16.200
You know everybody is socially distanced

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.140
or physically distanced.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.175
- Yeah.
- However you want to say it.

00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:21.306
And people, we all get COVID tested.

00:00:21.306 --> 00:00:23.080
It's great comedians.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.190
I mean, I've from Sarah Silverman,

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:30.036
then Tiffany Haddish, to my
man Muhammad to Dave himself

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:33.190
it's like some of the best comedians.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.160
Michael Che, Jon Hamm was out there.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.100
We had a great time,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.555
but we also performed Questlove
from the roots Erykah Badu.

00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:42.770
And it felt so great to be on stage.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.750
It's like you remember the joy

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.630
of what it is when you're on stage.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.140
Like not only the joy for you,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.870
but the joy you able to give people.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.703
I think that's,

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:53.664
I mean I don't know for you,
- Yeah.

00:00:53.664 --> 00:00:57.080
but for me being on stage
is like you sharing a gift.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:57.913
- it's you're the vessel.

00:00:57.913 --> 00:00:59.230
- Your the vessel

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.310
and you receive energy from the crowd,

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.860
but you also give energy.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.420
So it was just a blessing to be there,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.460
we all were like energized
by getting on stage.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.293
- Were y'all all on it.

00:01:08.293 --> 00:01:09.630
Like this is my dream movie

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.030
of all the people that you just said.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.500
So were we you all on stage
at certain points together?

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.570
Like doing stuff together.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.403
- Yeah we were together

00:01:15.403 --> 00:01:17.790
because as soon as we
arrived in yellow Springs,

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.530
you get COVID tests.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.718
And so at that point we
get our little wristband

00:01:21.718 --> 00:01:23.405
- Am getting the band.

00:01:23.405 --> 00:01:24.238
and I'm good.

00:01:24.238 --> 00:01:27.600
And everybody feels a
little more comfortable.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.170
It's you know it's a
transition for people because,

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.020
you know we all coming from the world

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.390
where we like wearing a mask,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.280
but once we got COVID tested,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.934
it's a small amount of people that around.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:40.310
And you know, but it's a great crowd.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:43.530
Like everybody and people come
from all over the Midwest.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.180
Mostly Ohio and Yellow
Springs is a great town.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.400
Shout out to yellow Springs.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.233
I love this town.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:49.493
(crowd cheering)

00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:51.940
It's like a hippie town
in the middle of Ohio,

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.970
small place and Dave is like the mirror.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:54.803
- Very artistic.

00:01:54.803 --> 00:01:55.840
- Yeah it's very artistic.
- Yeah.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.610
I bought Palo Santo

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:59.470
and different little antique things there.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.480
I love it.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.380
- That's so cool.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.891
And what a, what a way to
navigate what's going on.

00:02:03.891 --> 00:02:04.724
- Yeah.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:05.557
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:05.557 --> 00:02:07.220
Like for it not to
completely stop everyone

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.370
and their creativity and their expression

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.410
and inspiring people.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.010
That's, that's a really,
really cool way to do that.

